(ROOT/'metadata/ADAPTATIONS_ZH.md').write_text('# Adaptations fixed before test scoring\n1. Import upstream SAITS.impute directly, retaining both DMSA modules and attention-weighted fusion. Do not use the upstream all-variable forward loss. Supervise only the query target: hidden-target MAE plus mean visible-target reconstruction MAE across three outputs, each weighted 1. Two layers means 2 layers per DMSA module.\n2. To avoid unequal training steps from independent early stopping, pair branches with the same model seed. Stop together only after both have failed to improve for 8 consecutive epochs, up to 50 epochs. Each checkpoint is still selected on D05. The earlier-stagnating branch may train longer; this is a budget-fairness adaptation, not original independent early stopping.\n3. Comparison models retain 24-dimensional shapes and identical parameter counts. H retains visible query-target values only; M hides the specified collection group. The input interface contains only X and missing_mask.\n4. Recovery stratification uses archived episode end to end_exclusion as a recovery-exclusion proxy, not certification of physical recovery. Unmarked periods are called normal background, without guaranteeing absence of unknown faults.\n5. Original values and predictions are saved in native units in parquet; displayed bitrate is divided by 1e6. Standardization scales are estimated once from original D01–D04 rows, without overlap weighting.\n6. Execution uses the existing PyTorch 2.11 environment rather than reconstructing 2023 dependencies. This is a task-adapted SAITS implementation, not a claimed reproduction of the original paper.\n')
